{"name":"Thistle Down","hex":"#9499bb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thistle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several perennial composite plants, especially of genera Cirsium, Carduus, Cynara, or Onopordum, having prickly leaves and showy flower heads with prickly bracts.","This plant seen as the national emblem of Scotland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thistle"},{"term":"down","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["From a higher position to a lower one; downwards.","To or towards what is considered the bottom of something, irrespective of whether this is presently physically lower."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["From the higher end to the lower of.","From north to south of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thistle","blocks":[{"text":"Thistle is the popular name of a group of flowering plants characterised by leaves with sharp spikes on the margins, mostly in the family Asteraceae. Prickles can also occur all over the plant – on the stem, and on the flat parts of the leaves. These prickles protect the plant from herbivores. Typically, an involucre with a clasping shape, similar to a cup or urn, subtends each of a thistle's flower heads. The typically feathery pappus of a ripe thistle flower is known as thistle-down."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg/330px-Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thistle"},{"title":"Thistledown (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Thistledown is a 1938 British musical film directed by Arthur B. Woods and starring Aino Bergo, Keith Falkner, Athole Stewart, Sharon Lynn and Amy Veness. it was written Brock Williams from a story by J.O.C. Orton and John Meehan Jr, and produced by Irving Asher."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Thistledown_film_frame_%281938%29_130926-231843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thistledown_(film)"},{"title":"Shades of purple","blocks":[{"text":"There are numerous variations of the color purple, a sampling of which is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shades_of_Purple.svg/330px-Shades_of_Purple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg/500px-Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg/1280px-Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg/500px-Milk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Milk thistle flowerhead","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilk_thistle_flowerhead.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Red_Thistle.JPG/500px-Red_Thistle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Red_Thistle.JPG/1280px-Red_Thistle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Red_Thistle.JPG/500px-Red_Thistle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cirsium arizonicum, showing arachnoid cobwebbiness on stems and leaves, with ants attending aphids that might be taking advantage of the shelter.","link":"https